Type Conversion:
implicit conversion: when a value of one type is automatically converted to another
explicit conversion: when a value of one type is manually converted using casting

int x = 3.14;

std::cout << x; // prints 3, because the decimal is truncated

double x = (int) 3.14; // explicit conversion, x is now 3.0

char x = 100; // implicit conversion, x is now 'd' because 100 is the ASCII value for 'd'

std::cout << (char) 100; //explicit conversion, prints 'd'


