Switches:

switches are used tocompare a variable to multiple values and execute different code based on the value.
It makes it so that you don't have to write multiple if statements.
Write default: in place of case to execute code if none of the cases match the variable.
int main() {

    int month;
    std::cout << "Enter the month (1-12): ";
    std::cin >> month;

    switch(month) {
        case 1:
            std::cout << "January";
            break;
        case 2:
            std::cout << "February";
            break;
        case 3:
            std::cout << "March";
            break;
        default:
            std::cout << "Invalid month";
            break;
    }
}


