Break and Continue:

for(int i = 1; i<=20; i++) {
    if (i == 10) {
        break; // breaks out of the loop when i is 10
    }}

for(int i = 1; i <= 20; i++)
{
    if (i == 10) {
        continue; // skips the rest of the loop when i is 10
    }
    std::cout << i << std::endl;
}

When would this be important: When you need to exit a loop early or skip something based on the condtions.

